iversary Timeline Portraits of Ursuline College People 150th Celebration Photos Office of the President Board of Trustees Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Overview For the Media Brand Guide Contact Overview Accreditation Campus Security Policies, Crime Statistics and Crime Log Data Request Consumer Complaint Process Education Unit Completer Reporting Measures HEERF Report Professional Licensure and Certification Disclosures Title IX Compliance Back Overview Learning Outcomes Literacies Common Courses Distribution Courses Credit & Evaluation Overview Home / Inside Ursuline / Employment / Job Opportunities / Associate Director of Admissions | Ursuline - Liberal Arts College in OH Employment Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Calendar News Documents & Forms Employment Job Opportunities Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Calendar News Documents & Forms Apply Now Visit Ursuline Find a Program Request Info « back to jobs list Associate Director of Admissions Full-Time / Posted September 23, 2026 Summary The Ursuline College Campus of Gannon University seeks an experienced enrollment professional to serve as an Associate Director of Admissions. This position is responsible for recruiting prospective students, primarily throughout Northeast Ohio, to undergraduate programs while also supporting significant administrative functions within the Office of Admissions. Responsibilities include planning small-group campus visits; assisting with open house and other admission events; training and supporting admission counselors; coordinating counselor travel; assisting with admission marketing materials; and overseeing counselor activity and reporting within Slate, the customer relationship management (CRM) system. This position is full-time, on-campus, reporting to the Director of Undergraduate Admission. Responsibilities Recruit prospective students for undergraduate programs within an assigned territory, primarily in Northeast Ohio. Develop and maintain relationships with prospective students, families, high school counselors, community organizations, and other constituents. Plan and coordinate small group campus visits and assist with open house and other admission events. Support the training, coaching, and professional development of admission counselors. Coordinate counselor travel and recruitment schedules. Assist with the development and implementation of admission marketing materials and communications. Monitor counselor activity, reports, and recruitment data in Slate. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; master’s degree preferred. A minimum of 3 to 4 years of admissions or student recruitment experience required. Experience at a small, private liberal arts institution preferred. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in an inclusive and diverse community. Excellent interpersonal, written communication, presentation, and public-speaking skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office. Experience with Technolutions’ Slate CRM preferred. Valid driver’s license and ability to travel as required. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends. How to Apply Interested candidates should use the form below or email letter of interest, resume, and salary requirements to Kelly.tomory@gannon.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. Apply to this position First Name Last Name Phone Email Resume Cover Letter Comments Submit Inside Ursuline News Ursuline College named Center of Excellence in Nursing Education Learn More ‘Change of Control’ approved in Gannon-Ursuline merger Learn More US News Rankings tops a week of accomplishments for The Breen School of Nursing & Health Professions Learn More Events NOV 14 Discover Nursing Day 2550 Lander Rd Pepper Pike, OH 44124 888 URSULINE or 440 449 4200 Contact Footer Quick Links Quick Navigation Why Ursuline Admission Academics Student Life Cost & Aid Athletics Calendar News Directory Map Inside Ursuline Library Wasmer Gallery Alumni Employment Give Apply Connect Programs Info Why Ursuline Admission Academics Student Life Cost & Aid Athletics Calendar News Directory Map Inside Ursuline Library Wasmer Gallery Alumni Employment Give MY URSULINE EMAIL D2L DOCS, DOWNLOADS & FORMS Consumer Information Privacy Policy ©2026 Ursuline College. All rights reserved."
    },
