 Overview Our Sponsors 150th Anniversary Timeline Portraits of Ursuline College People 150th Celebration Photos Office of the President Board of Trustees Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Overview For the Media Brand Guide Contact Overview Accreditation Campus Security Policies, Crime Statistics and Crime Log Data Request Consumer Complaint Process Education Unit Completer Reporting Measures HEERF Report Professional Licensure and Certification Disclosures Title IX Compliance Back Overview Learning Outcomes Literacies Common Courses Distribution Courses Credit & Evaluation Overview Home / Inside Ursuline / Employment / Job Opportunities / Maintenance Worker | Ursuline - Liberal Arts College in OH Employment Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Calendar News Documents & Forms Employment Job Opportunities Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Calendar News Documents & Forms Apply Now Visit Ursuline Find a Program Request Info « back to jobs list Maintenance Worker Full-Time / Posted August 27, 2026 Summary Maintain and repair college equipment, facilities, and grounds.  This position requires the ability to have full bodily movement for activities, including the ability to repair machinery by hand and to maintain the grounds by hand.  The work schedule is Tuesday through Saturday (Sundays/Mondays are days off).  Availability for on-call work for emergencies during off hours, including snow removal. Responsibilities Work from work order requests, verbal, electronic and written instructions, including tracking, completion & close-out of all service and PM work orders. Install wiring and lighting hardware; replace ballasts, fixtures, motors, pumps, re-building of pump seals and other equipment; install or repair faucets, sinks, waterlines, and other plumbing equipment. Maintain water treatment system; check water clarity and record readings; wash down and clean equipment. Check system lines for leaks or malfunctions; make repairs. Maintain facility appearance; repair and paint walls and other structures; replace tile, roofing, windows; move furniture, build shelves. Maintain grounds appearance; plow snow, salt sidewalks; remove debris and rubbish; patch parking areas and roads; insure hazard free conditions. Make pickups and deliveries on and off campus of packages, supplies, and other items; operate vehicles in a safe manner observing rules and laws of the road. Perform preventive maintenance on equipment, vehicles, and machinery; inspect fire extinguishers, sprinkler systems, other safety equipment. Exercise proper care in the use of tools, equipment, and materials; complete maintenance records and sign off. Detect and report faulty equipment, defective material, improper operations, and unusual conditions to supervision. Attend and participate in department training including van training. Provide day-time security activities. Observe all prescribed safety rules and regulations. Maintain work areas in a neat and orderly condition. Collect and transport to containers, refuse and recycling. Qualifications High school education or equivalent plus two (2) years related experience.  Basic knowledge of HVAC, plumbing and electrical systems.  Ability to handle the physical demands of the job including standing, bending, pulling, pushing, climbing and lifting up to 50lbs.   Effective communication skills.  Must have a valid driver’s license and a clean driving record.  Available to work required OT. How to Apply Interested candidates should use the form below or email letter of interest, resume, and salary requirements to kknaus@ursuline.edu.  Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. Apply to this position First Name Last Name Phone Email Resume Cover Letter Comments Submit Inside Ursuline News Ursuline College named Center of Excellence in Nursing Education Learn More ‘Change of Control’ approved in Gannon-Ursuline merger Learn More US News Rankings tops a week of accomplishments for The Breen School of Nursing & Health Professions Learn More Events NOV 14 Discover Nursing Day 2550 Lander Rd Pepper Pike, OH 44124 888 URSULINE or 440 449 4200 Contact Footer Quick Links Quick Navigation Why Ursuline Admission Academics Student Life Cost & Aid Athletics Calendar News Directory Map Inside Ursuline Library Wasmer Gallery Alumni Employment Give Apply Connect Programs Info Why Ursuline Admission Academics Student Life Cost & Aid Athletics Calendar News Directory Map Inside Ursuline Library Wasmer Gallery Alumni Employment Give MY URSULINE EMAIL D2L DOCS, DOWNLOADS & FORMS Consumer Information Privacy Policy ©2026 Ursuline College. All rights reserved."
    },
