Graduate Students Welcome + Overview Our Sponsors 150th Anniversary Timeline Portraits of Ursuline College People 150th Celebration Photos Office of the President Board of Trustees Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Overview For the Media Brand Guide Contact Overview Accreditation Campus Security Policies, Crime Statistics and Crime Log Data Request Consumer Complaint Process Education Unit Completer Reporting Measures HEERF Report Professional Licensure and Certification Disclosures Title IX Compliance Back Overview Learning Outcomes Literacies Common Courses Distribution Courses Credit & Evaluation Overview Home / Inside Ursuline / Employment / Job Opportunities / Adjunct Faculty, Exercise Science Department  | Ursuline - Liberal Arts College in OH Employment Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Calendar News Documents & Forms Employment Job Opportunities Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Calendar News Documents & Forms Apply Now Visit Ursuline Find a Program Request Info « back to jobs list Adjunct Faculty, Exercise Science Department Part-Time / Posted August 13, 2026 Summary Adjunct faculty will share their knowledge and mentor students in the discipline of exercise physiology where the effects of physical activity affect physiological systems of the human population. Adjunct faculty member will teach the Exercise Physiology lecture and associated laboratory courses in the undergraduate Exercise Science program at Ursuline College Campus of Gannon University. Responsibilities Adjunct faculty member will be expected to: Develop and disseminate traditional face-to-face lectures to address course learning objectives Prepare and facilitate laboratory activities to address course learning objectives Evaluate and grade assignments and assessments and provide to students in a timely manner Manage (at minimum) the grade book using the online learning management system (D2L Brightspace) Respond to students promptly and positively to support them in an inclusive environment Courses include: EXS 270: Exercise Physiology EXS 270L: Exercise Physiology Lab (*two sections) Appointment Term single-term Appointment Credits 7 Delivery Method face-to-face (in-person) Qualifications Master’s degree or higher from an accredited academic institution in Exercise Physiology or related discipline (e.g., Exercise Science, etc.) required. Preferred qualifications include previous university-level teaching experience in exercise physiology; Exercise Physiologist certification and/or laboratory experience in exercise physiology; adult CPR/AED certified. How to Apply Qualified candidates should complete the form below or send cover letter and curriculum vita to scott.willis@gannon.edu .  Review of materials will begin immediately and will continue until positions are filled. Apply to this position First Name Last Name Phone Email Resume Cover Letter Comments Submit Inside Ursuline News Ursuline College named Center of Excellence in Nursing Education Learn More ‘Change of Control’ approved in Gannon-Ursuline merger Learn More US News Rankings tops a week of accomplishments for The Breen School of Nursing & Health Professions Learn More Events NOV 14 Discover Nursing Day 2550 Lander Rd Pepper Pike, OH 44124 888 URSULINE or 440 449 4200 Contact Footer Quick Links Quick Navigation Why Ursuline Admission Academics Student Life Cost & Aid Athletics Calendar News Directory Map Inside Ursuline Library Wasmer Gallery Alumni Employment Give Apply Connect Programs Info Why Ursuline Admission Academics Student Life Cost & Aid Athletics Calendar News Directory Map Inside Ursuline Library Wasmer Gallery Alumni Employment Give MY URSULINE EMAIL D2L DOCS, DOWNLOADS & FORMS Consumer Information Privacy Policy ©2026 Ursuline College. All rights reserved."
    },
