w Our Sponsors 150th Anniversary Timeline Portraits of Ursuline College People 150th Celebration Photos Office of the President Board of Trustees Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Overview For the Media Brand Guide Contact Overview Accreditation Campus Security Policies, Crime Statistics and Crime Log Data Request Consumer Complaint Process Education Unit Completer Reporting Measures HEERF Report Professional Licensure and Certification Disclosures Title IX Compliance Back Overview Learning Outcomes Literacies Common Courses Distribution Courses Credit & Evaluation Overview Home / Inside Ursuline / Employment / Job Opportunities / Coordinator for Grants, Sponsored Programs, and Research | Ursuline - Liberal Arts College in OH Employment Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Calendar News Documents & Forms Employment Job Opportunities Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Calendar News Documents & Forms Apply Now Visit Ursuline Find a Program Request Info « back to jobs list Coordinator for Grants, Sponsored Programs, and Research Full-Time / Posted August 12, 2026 Summary The Coordinator functions as a grant officer and provides assistance in carrying out the mission of the Office of Sponsored Programs and Research (OSPR). This position aids in securing external funding opportunities, educating Ursuline College Campus and the Gannon University community about grant procedures, assisting them in the planning, preparation, and submission of grant proposals. The Coordinator supports all phases of grant operations, including clerical and administrative duties. Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Responsibilities: Monitor government and foundation websites for funding opportunities.  Create and disseminate solicitation summaries to align internal interests with opportunities. Work independently with internal and external stakeholders as part of proposal writing teams. Collaborate with Ursuline College Campus leadership, faculty, and staff regularly. Prepare and submit sponsor forms and lead overall proposal submission to ensure a complete, compliant, and cohesive submission package. Provide grant education and training for faculty/staff through live and/or recorded sessions. Maintain user access and authorization for grant application portals including grants.gov, research.gov, and foundational portal submission sites. Maintain file of institutional documents including, but not limited to, board of trustee list, 501c3 status, indirect cost rate agreements, facilities statements and data management plans. Develop and maintain a grant and report calendar to track and schedule grant proposals, progress reports, and internal and external reports. Provide guidance and follow-up to ensure post-award reporting requirements are met, using the office’s tracking system. Make decisions related to the OSPR in the absence of the Director. Manage office operations and maintains portal site. Perform other duties as assigned within the scope, responsibility and requirements of the position and informed by Gannon’s Mission and shared values. Required Qualifications Education: A bachelor’s degree is required. Experience:  Two or more years of grant-related experience. Must possess the following skills: excellent written, verbal, proofreading and organizational skills; the ability to read written instructions and procedure manuals; the ability to enter data into records, logs and websites with accuracy; the ability to prioritize responsibilities, seek direction regarding courses of action; and the ability to research and compile qualitative and quantitative data. The ability to work independently and manage projects. The ability to be effective while reporting to a supervisor and divisional team that are positioned across multiple campuses. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education is preferred. How to Apply Please click the following link to learn more details about the position and to apply by submitting your resume and a cover letter: https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14893 Inside Ursuline News Ursuline College named Center of Excellence in Nursing Education Learn More ‘Change of Control’ approved in Gannon-Ursuline merger Learn More US News Rankings tops a week of accomplishments for The Breen School of Nursing & Health Professions Learn More Events NOV 14 Discover Nursing Day 2550 Lander Rd Pepper Pike, OH 44124 888 URSULINE or 440 449 4200 Contact Footer Quick Links Quick Navigation Why Ursuline Admission Academics Student Life Cost & Aid Athletics Calendar News Directory Map Inside Ursuline Library Wasmer Gallery Alumni Employment Give Apply Connect Programs Info Why Ursuline Admission Academics Student Life Cost & Aid Athletics Calendar News Directory Map Inside Ursuline Library Wasmer Gallery Alumni Employment Give MY URSULINE EMAIL D2L DOCS, DOWNLOADS & FORMS Consumer Information Privacy Policy ©2026 Ursuline College. All rights reserved."
