erview Our Sponsors 150th Anniversary Timeline Portraits of Ursuline College People 150th Celebration Photos Office of the President Board of Trustees Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Overview For the Media Brand Guide Contact Overview Accreditation Campus Security Policies, Crime Statistics and Crime Log Data Request Consumer Complaint Process Education Unit Completer Reporting Measures HEERF Report Professional Licensure and Certification Disclosures Title IX Compliance Back Overview Learning Outcomes Literacies Common Courses Distribution Courses Credit & Evaluation Overview Home / Inside Ursuline / Employment / Job Opportunities / Nursing Faculty | Ursuline - Liberal Arts College in OH Employment Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Calendar News Documents & Forms Employment Job Opportunities Overview Job Opportunities Benefits Calendar News Documents & Forms Apply Now Visit Ursuline Find a Program Request Info « back to jobs list Nursing Faculty Full-Time / Posted July 31, 2026 Summary The Breen School of Nursing invites applications for nine-month and twelve-month full-time faculty positions in both the Undergraduate and Graduate Nursing Programs. Rank is commensurate with experience and the positions are available immediately. Responsibilities Maintaining expertise within content and clinical areas taught as well as state of the art teaching practices; Developing the course syllabus according to the course description and objectives approved by the undergraduate faculty; teaching classes and preparing all assessment methodologies; documenting student issues; updating the use of textbooks and other readings and electronic resources as necessary; serving as an course coordinator, academic advisor and clinical instructor to assigned students; attending all School meetings, assigned subcommittees, and other Campus/University meetings. Qualifications 1. Doctoral Degree (DNP, PhD, EdD) required to teach in the Graduate Program. 2. Master’s Degree with a major in nursing required to teach in the Undergraduate Program. 3. Two years of experience in the practice of nursing as a registered nurse, five years preferred. 4. At least one year of experience as a faculty member in a registered nursing education program (pre-licensure), preferred. 5. Must qualify for a faculty appointment and have an unencumbered RN license to practice nursing in Ohio. How to Apply Qualified candidates should use form below or send letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and three letters of reference to Dr. Sarahbeth Abalos at Sarahbeth.abalos@gannon.edu. Review of applications to begin immediately and will continue until position is filled. Apply to this position First Name Last Name Phone Email Resume Cover Letter Comments Submit Inside Ursuline News Ursuline College named Center of Excellence in Nursing Education Learn More ‘Change of Control’ approved in Gannon-Ursuline merger Learn More US News Rankings tops a week of accomplishments for The Breen School of Nursing & Health Professions Learn More Events NOV 14 Discover Nursing Day 2550 Lander Rd Pepper Pike, OH 44124 888 URSULINE or 440 449 4200 Contact Footer Quick Links Quick Navigation Why Ursuline Admission Academics Student Life Cost & Aid Athletics Calendar News Directory Map Inside Ursuline Library Wasmer Gallery Alumni Employment Give Apply Connect Programs Info Why Ursuline Admission Academics Student Life Cost & Aid Athletics Calendar News Directory Map Inside Ursuline Library Wasmer Gallery Alumni Employment Give MY URSULINE EMAIL D2L DOCS, DOWNLOADS & FORMS Consumer Information Privacy Policy ©2026 Ursuline College. All rights reserved."
